    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes (260 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an email-uniqueness check to `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`. When a new owner is created, the controller now compares the request's lower-cased email against the lower-cased email of every existing owner, and returns **409 Conflict** if a match is found.\n\nThe check:\n- Runs only when an email is provided (a `null` email is not considered \"in use\").\n- Case-insensitively compares against all existing owners, skipping owners with no email.\n- Mirrors the existing duplicate-telephone `CONFLICT` pattern and is placed right after it, before the record is persisted.\n\nSince emails are already stored lower-cased (`owner.setEmail(email == null ? null : email.toLowerCase())`), the comparison is consistent with stored data, and the pre-existing email format validation (400) still runs first.",
